## Findings

Both are late findings. The suggested call for each is tech-debt, because each names test tooling or a record, not a product file.

ADV-31 [Late finding; note; suggested call tech-debt]
  In src/__tests__/blog-posts-loader.adversarial.test.ts, mkdirSync and symlinkSync run between mkdtempSync and the try block.
  If either call throws, the finally block never runs and the temp base stays in the OS temp directory (Q5).
  The sibling helper postsTree() in blog-posts-loader-symlink.test.ts:30-35 has the same shape.
  The folder is small and sits in the OS temp directory. Moving the two calls inside the try block removes the leak.

ADV-32 [Late finding; note; record precision; suggested call tech-debt]
  The tech-debt row of dc9d39dac and plan task 4.15 summarize ADV-26 and ADV-27 too broadly.
  ADV-26 says "weak non-English guards". The clause removal also passes in en (P9 of adversarial-da99c46.log).
  ADV-27 says "APPROVED_SCHOOL_YEAR mutations pass". Changing the en or zh value fails the two real-copy label handoff tests (P4 of that log).
  Only the th value and the circular control pass.

